-## Real estate investing in Little River, SC
-Little River is the Grand Strand's northern, working-waterfront edge, just below the North Carolina line. It is built around the Intracoastal Waterway, a historic fishing village, and a pair of casino cruise boats. It offers a different value proposition from the beach towns: more affordable entry, genuine waterfront, and a growing year-round population rather than a pure tourism economy.
-For investors, Little River is increasingly a value and growth story. As pricing on the central and southern Strand has risen, buyers and renters have moved north. Little River's combination of lower entry points, waterway frontage, and new development has drawn primary residents, long-term tenants, and a measure of vacation demand. It rewards investors who want coastal exposure without prime-beach pricing.
