-## The Myrtle Beach market right now
-Myrtle Beach is a condo-heavy market, so a single median can mislead. City-wide figures land anywhere from the high $180,000s to the mid $310,000s depending on the source, because condos pull the number down and single-family homes push it up. As a reference point, Zillow put the city home-value index near $315,000 in early 2026, down about 3 percent year over year. Single-family homes commonly run in the $330,000s to high $380,000s. The ZIP codes range from about $275,000 in 29577 to about $354,000 in 29579. The condo segment carries the most inventory and the most negotiating room. For an accurate figure on the exact segment you want, we pull the Coastal Carolinas MLS.
