-## Where Pawleys Island sits, and how it is governed
-Pawleys Island is a Georgetown County market about 25 miles south of Myrtle Beach and one of the oldest summer resorts on the East Coast, known for its understated "arrogantly shabby" character. It has two parts that matter for buyers. One is the small incorporated Town of Pawleys Island, which is the barrier island itself, a tiny town. The other is the larger unincorporated mainland, which includes Litchfield, Pawleys Plantation, Hagley Estates, The River Club, and, to the south, gated DeBordieu Colony.
